From: the jellyfin-ffmpeg contributors
Subject: allow qsvenc to bail out from unsupported low power mode
Origin: https://github.com/jellyfin/jellyfin-ffmpeg/blob/v8.1.3-2/debian/patches/0071-allow-qsvenc-to-bail-out-from-unsupported-low-power-mode.patch

The Quick Sync encoders leave low-power mode when the GPU refuses their
settings with it, instead of failing.

Rebased onto FFmpeg 9.0.2: the same change, at 9.0.2's line numbers.

From jellyfin-ffmpeg 8.1.3-2, where the patch has no header: its authors
are in that repository's history. Under FFmpeg's licence, as the files
it changes.
---
diff --git a/libavcodec/qsvenc.c b/libavcodec/qsvenc.c
--- a/libavcodec/qsvenc.c
+++ b/libavcodec/qsvenc.c
@@ -693,6 +693,13 @@ static int check_enc_param(AVCodecContex
               av_log(avctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "Current resolution is unsupported\n");
         if (UNMATCH(FrameInfo.FourCC))
               av_log(avctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "Current pixel format is unsupported\n");
+        /* bail out from the error caused by unsupported Low power mode */
+        if (q->param.mfx.LowPower == MFX_CODINGOPTION_ON) {
+            av_log(avctx, AV_LOG_WARNING, "Some encoding parameters are not supported "
+                   "under Low power mode, trying to recover with it set to disabled\n");
+            q->param.mfx.LowPower = MFX_CODINGOPTION_UNKNOWN;
+            return check_enc_param(avctx, q);
+        }
         return 0;
     }
     return 1;
